  body: "# UK capital: valuation basis and deductions\n\n**Model-assisted source interpretation; unreviewed.
    No entitlement decision or executable rule.**\n\nThe captured paragraph uses current market or surrender
    value for capital in the UK and describes deductions for sale costs and secured encumbrances.\n\n\
    ## Evidence and scope\n\n[DMG 84692, PDF page 92](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/6a5e38bb8b7e4fa537e693d5/dmg-ch84.pdf#page=92)
    supports this scoped proposal. The source PDF SHA-256 is `f5c610b29bdb81e11736409b7f33ccf7917a4d8945f2821802801073e0d753ee`.\n\
    \nThis concept supplies no asset valuation or award calculation. Regulation 19, cited decisions and
    the surrounding valuation guidance require review.\n\nThe capture date, the publication page's update
    date and a date stated in the guidance have different meanings. Linked legislation and memos need
    their own provision, version and applicability review.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/capital-valuation
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: This is an explicit valuation basis within the capital-valuation topic. Geographic
      scope, conditional sale costs and secured debts remain part of the statement.
    evidence:
    - page: page/84/0092
      quote: "84692 The value of capital which a person has in the UK (see DMG 070880), is its current
        market or\nsurrender value less\n\n\n1. 10% of the value if there are costs of sale and\n\n\n\
        2. the amount of any encumbrance secured on the capital1.\n\n\n                              \
        \                                 1 SPC Regs, reg 19, R(SB) 2/83, CJSA 3067/09"
      locator: DMG 84692
